        <h2>Summary / Description</h2>
        <div class="description">
          OBJECTIVES:<br> 
The MK I rower provided a means of demonstrating the feasibility of rowing as a form of
in-flight exercise. Recommendations from the crew who used the MK I rower have been
implemented for this extended duration orbiter (EDO) rower ergometer. In addition,
software control has been implemented to improve aerobic and resistive exercise
capabilities. The electronic display allowed for immediate feedback to the subject
regarding workload during the session and corresponding heart rate. The memory card is
capable of providing the unique rowing and resistive exercise protocol for each subject as
well as a data storage medium for postflight analysis. The aerobic and resistive exercise
capability of the EDO rower ergometer was evaluated for use in future in-flight exercise
prescriptions.
<p>
The objectives of this study were :<br>
1. Evaluate the rower for ease of set up and stowage, and physical comfort during
rowing exercise.<br>
2. Demonstrate the rower's ability to deliver quantifiable workloads in both rowing and
resistive exercise modes.<br>
3. Evaluate the rower in various configurations for resistive exercise capability in
microgravity.<br>
<p>
APPROACH:<br> 
Video of the subject rowing session and resistive exercise session are required. Head-to-toe
view of the subject is requested. Five minutes duration for each session is requested.
Documentary 35 millimeter (mm) still photos are requested of a rowing session and
resistive exercise session.
<p>
The rower ergometer system was stowed either in a middeck locker or on a
mounting frame. a device which attaches to the middeck floor.<br>
Configuration 1:<br>
When stowed in a locker, the rower ergometer was unstowed from the locker on
orbit and attached directly to a pair of middeck floor studs. The rower accessories
were unstowed from the locker and attached to the rower ergometer.<br>
Configuration 2:<br>
When stowed on the mounting frame, the rower ergometer was unstowed from the
mounting frame and attached to the middeck floor studs. The rower ergometer
accessories were unstowed from the accessory bag and attached to the rower
ergometer. The interface fixture and accessory bag were stowed on-orbit until the entire rower
ergometer system was configured for landing. The rower ergometer did not have to be
stowed after each exercise session.
<p>
All exercise sessions were controlled and recorded using the credit card memory
system located inside the rower. The heart rate chest strap was worn prior to and
during each session. A voice activated recorder was used for comments after the
session.
<p>
For rowing exercise: The subject performed two exercise sessions in the rowing
exercise mode (one interval protocol and one steady-state protocol). Each flight day
(FD), the subject strapped into the foot plates and performed warm ups, conditioning,
and cool down phases of exercise as controlled by the rower. 
<p>
For resistive exercise: The subject configured the rower and performed five
repetitions of the following exercises; squat, biceps curl, overhead press, calf raises,
and upright rowing. Various configurations for the same exercise were requested to
determine the optimal setup. Individual maximum workloads for resistive exercises
were predetermined and controlled by the credit card memory. Written comments
were be put into the checklist under the diagrams of the different configurations for
resistive exercise.
<p>
RESULTS:<br>                        
Results for this study aren’t available.
<p>
